#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "486cc512-416b-5eac-8964-1a87d533de72" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Given Set Is Linearly Independent Given Information on Its Elements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec04b5d0-1115-5135-a55c-7386bf8b0701" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304609} {:answer/id #uuid "ac1ec7fc-ddbc-5324-ba4a-c281bcdf11b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304610} {:answer/id #uuid "d82aa59a-aaab-5a3a-8b60-fb2fc5018a95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304611} {:answer/id #uuid "2f764ff7-c5fc-5f5d-9f16-b23afe8ac61f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304612} {:answer/id #uuid "d6775869-23e7-53c9-a3e9-ce7caec0e08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f764ff7-c5fc-5f5d-9f16-b23afe8ac61f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304612} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba2e8c1c-d628-5743-8d86-c18a87fd2bfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c84911ef-2785-567d-be2c-a7fe2c0d528f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107043" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},2{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent\n- ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent\n- ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}}$ is linearly independent" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({v}_{1}+{v}_{3})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}+{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}(2{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1}+{v}_{3},{v}_{2}+{v}_{3},2{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, ${x}_{1}{v}_{2}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}=0$ must have only the zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$  If this equation has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{2}+b\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\n0\\cdot {v}_{1}+a\\cdot {v}_{2}+b\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {v}_{1}+1\\cdot {v}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot ({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. In general, any set containing the zero vector is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}]}
